WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.710
Hi, welcome back to
Nagarjuna, Part Three.

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:05.883
And we've reached Chapter 15,

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.740
which is called "An Investigation
of a Nature to Things."

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.450
In Tibetan, we can see here,

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.130
it's called RANG BZHIN BRTAG PA

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:17.560
RANG BZHIN BRTAG PA

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.781
BRTAG PA means PARIKSHA which means...

00:00:20.781 --> 00:00:21.791
- [Woman] Investigation.

00:00:21.791 --> 00:00:23.360
- An investigation.

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.394
RANG BZHIN is an interesting word

00:00:25.394 --> 00:00:28.210
because it means "its own face".

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:30.055
BZHIN here means face.

00:00:30.055 --> 00:00:32.330
BZHIN RAS which means face.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:35.060
So RANG BZHIN means
"the face" of something,

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:39.040
which means its nature, which means...

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.710
And get it straight at
the beginning, okay?

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:46.486
It means the identity of
something: the inherent nature.

00:00:46.486 --> 00:00:50.012
Some quality of a thing
which is inside of it.

00:00:50.012 --> 00:00:52.430
So you've got to get this feeling of...

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:55.580
We're going to investigate
whether or not, for example,

00:00:55.580 --> 00:01:00.090
fire has an identity or
a nature inside of it

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:04.380
of being hot and then that
nature kind of opens up

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:06.980
and expresses itself in the world.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:11.860
Does fire have a nature
inside of it which is hot?

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:13.900
And then somehow the fire opens up

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:16.110
and the hotness comes out.

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:18.770
Does it have its own identity?

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:21.130
So when we say nature here,

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:25.820
or svabhāva (svabhava),
RANG BZHIN, think about,

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:28.540
it's sort of a thing deep
down inside of a thing

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:30.080
which is it's true identity.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.160
Think of identity.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:35.700
All right, here we go to our arguments.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:39.250
First verse.

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:41.629
First verse and a half.

00:01:41.629 --> 00:01:42.987
,RANG BZHIN RGYU DANG RKYEN LAS NI,

00:01:42.987 --> 00:01:46.478
,'BYUNG BAR RIGS PA MA YIN NO,

00:01:46.478 --> 00:01:48.620
,RGYU DANG RKYEN LAS BYUNG BA YI,

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:51.753
,RANG BZHIN BYAS PA CAN DU 'GYUR,

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:54.720
If you think about it,

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:57.820
if something's identity is part of it,

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:00.758
it shouldn't have to be created.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:07.510
If the identity of an
object is inherent to it,

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:10.070
which is what identity means,

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:12.110
it shouldn't be something that you get

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:15.131
only if something else happens.

00:02:15.131 --> 00:02:17.075
You're just born with it.

00:02:17.075 --> 00:02:18.160
You just come with it.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.094
Nobody has to heat up a fire.

00:02:20.094 --> 00:02:22.066
[hands rubbing]

00:02:22.066 --> 00:02:23.590
Fire is already hot.

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:26.950
So if it were the case that
you had to do something to make

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:30.583
the fire hot, then hot
wouldn't be the nature of fire.

00:02:31.642 --> 00:02:33.923
- Are we agreed? - Yeah.

00:02:33.923 --> 00:02:36.590
If you had to do something else,

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:40.360
if you had to light a fire
under a fire to make it hot,

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.440
then the nature of the fire,

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:44.880
we wouldn't say hot is
the nature of the fire.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:48.710
So we can say something
about nature or identity.

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:50.480
It comes with the thing,

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:52.430
and it's not something that comes about

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:54.000
if other things are there,

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.283
if other causes and conditions are there.

00:02:57.283 --> 00:02:59.341
,RANG BZHIN RGYU DANG RKYEN LAS NI,

00:02:59.341 --> 00:03:02.166
,'BYUNG BAR RIGS PA MA YIN NO,

00:03:02.166 --> 00:03:07.100
It would be improper to say
that something's self identity,

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:09.390
were only there if
something else happened,

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:12.090
some kinds of causes and conditions.

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:14.040
,RGYU DANG RKYEN LAS GANGS BYUNG BA YI,

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.865
,RANG BZHIN BYAS PA CAN DU 'GYUR,

00:03:16.865 --> 00:03:21.865
Because a nature which was
produced by other factors

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:26.840
and other causes would be artificial,

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:29.856
and artificial is the opposite of nature.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:36.070
It would be put together
and given to the fire.

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:38.480
Oh, here, let me heat you up.
[hands rubbing]

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:40.160
And then the fire gets hot.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:44.450
Then the nature wouldn't
be the nature in the fire.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:47.630
It would be produced artificially
and handed to the fire.

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:49.934
Okay, got it?

00:03:49.934 --> 00:03:51.050
RANG BZHIN BYAS PA CAN

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:53.393
So BYAS PA CAN here means

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.850
almost artificial, created.

00:03:58.225 --> 00:04:03.225
In the jewelry business, they
have real rubies and sapphires

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:05.783
and then they have fake ones.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:09.260
But when they learned
how to make real ruby

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:12.980
and sapphire in a laboratory,
they had a big debate about

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:15.110
whether to call it artificial or not.

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:17.280
And the guys who succeeded
in the process said

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:19.320
it's not artificial, it's real.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.020
And another guy said it's
not real if you don't

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:22.690
dig it out of the earth.

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:26.411
So they made a compromise and
they called it 'created ruby'.

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:32.790
And it sounds better than
artificial or substitute.

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:37.410
So if it's created, it's not natural.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.283
That's the point.

00:04:40.842 --> 00:04:43.360
RANG BZHIN BYAS PA CAN ZHES BYAR

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:48.330
If the self-nature of a thing,
or if the identity of a thing

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:50.912
has to be created from the outside,

00:04:50.912 --> 00:04:52.310
JI LTAR BUR NA RUNG BAR 'GYUR

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:55.210
then how the hell can
you call it a nature?

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:57.740
It's artificial, it's created.

00:04:57.740 --> 00:04:58.910
Got it?

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:01.410
Like created rubies.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:02.800
All right.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:04.560
Nagarjuna...

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:05.970
Now this is a story.

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:08.220
This picture has a story.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:12.273
So, my lama, I told you I was
a volunteer for my teacher

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:18.300
for 30 years, and about 25 of those years

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:23.300
I was his chauffeur from
New Jersey to Washington DC.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.920
It's a five hour drive.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.700
And he used to teach there once a month.

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:32.523
So I did that drive over 300 times.

00:05:34.485 --> 00:05:35.730
I drove him down there.

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:38.160
If you count both ways it's 600.

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:42.430
And so I knew all the road by my
heart and I enjoyed driving him

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:46.000
because he would always
refuse to answer my questions.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.220
And in the car, he couldn't refuse.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:52.565
He was locked in the car for five hours,

00:05:52.565 --> 00:05:55.730
and he ordered the car without a radio,

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:58.707
so I couldn't listen to the radio.

00:05:58.707 --> 00:06:01.667
And it costs extra money to
order the car without the radio.

00:06:01.667 --> 00:06:03.069
[laughter]

00:06:03.069 --> 00:06:06.353
So anyway, all you have to
do is talk about dharma.

00:06:06.353 --> 00:06:08.655
Then sometimes he would
pretend to be asleep.

00:06:08.655 --> 00:06:11.367
And I'd say I know you're not asleep.

00:06:11.367 --> 00:06:13.190
And he...
[imitates snoring]

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:18.190
Anyway, he used to always
stop at a Howard Johnson's

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:21.083
at the Maryland border, Delaware border,

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:23.840
just before the Delaware Bridge.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:26.010
We'd always stop at the same place,

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:28.630
and he would order his tea.

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:30.110
You know, he's a big tea drinker.

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:32.930
He drank about 15 cups of tea a day.

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:36.367
I made him 15-20 cups of tea a day.

00:06:36.367 --> 00:06:40.245
And they would try to give him creamer.

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:43.160
And he'd say, "No, I want cream.

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:45.218
"This is creamer. I don't want creamer.

00:06:45.218 --> 00:06:48.460
I want cream. I want the real thing."

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:50.110
And he taught me all these words

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:53.080
for artificial, fake, not natural.

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:57.570
All the words I learned from
him, which were all my words,

00:06:57.570 --> 00:06:58.870
they have a context.

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:00.910
We were sitting somewhere and he said,

00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:03.285
"This is called BCOS MA."

00:07:03.285 --> 00:07:04.326
BCOS MA means BYAS PA.

00:07:04.326 --> 00:07:06.750
BYAS PA means it had to be
created from the outside.

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:09.240
It's not natural.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:10.884
All right.

00:07:10.884 --> 00:07:13.075
And he hated this stuff,

00:07:13.942 --> 00:07:15.025
dearly.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:17.363
Okay.

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:22.545
Next verse. It's actually half a verse.

00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:25.657
And this is actually RANG LUGS.

00:07:25.657 --> 00:07:27.603
So what's that mean?

00:07:27.603 --> 00:07:30.069
This is our position.

00:07:30.069 --> 00:07:32.044
,RANG BZHIN DAG NI BCOS MIN DANG,

00:07:32.044 --> 00:07:34.490
,GZHAN LA LTOS PA MED PA YIN,

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:38.320
If something was a real identity,

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:40.398
it shouldn't be BCOS MA.

00:07:40.398 --> 00:07:43.990
BCOS MA means contrived
or artificially created.

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:46.050
It shouldn't be like the creamer.

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:48.248
It should just be real.

00:07:48.248 --> 00:07:50.983
BCOS MIN means not created.

00:07:50.983 --> 00:07:55.020
What's a famous BCOS PA in Lam Rim?

00:07:56.522 --> 00:07:58.640
BCOS MA?

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:00.206
That's where you try to feel like

00:08:00.206 --> 00:08:03.060
a bodhisattva when you're not.
[laughing]

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:05.060
That's a good BCOS MA.

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:07.493
All right. Fake bodhisattva.

00:08:08.570 --> 00:08:09.920
Created bodhisattva.

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:13.591
Artificial, you pretend
to be a bodhisattva,

00:08:13.591 --> 00:08:16.885
and then you're still messing
up all day, stuff like that.

00:08:16.885 --> 00:08:18.170
,GZHAN LA LTOS PA MED PA YIN,

00:08:18.170 --> 00:08:20.800
If something were a true nature,

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:23.190
it shouldn't have to
depend on any conditions

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:25.360
going around outside of it.

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:28.590
If fire is hot by nature,

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:31.280
it shouldn't matter where the fire is

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:33.430
or what's happening with the fire.

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:35.103
It should be hot from the inside.

00:08:35.103 --> 00:08:36.700
Something like it.

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:39.348
That's our definition of a nature.

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:44.590
And I was wondering, and maybe
you guys could think it over.

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:47.468
Is this BTAGS PA MTHA' BZUNG GI RIGS PA?

00:08:47.468 --> 00:08:49.670
Is this BTAGS PA MTHA' BZUNG GI RIGS PA?

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:52.230
And that's a very, very useful expression.

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:55.500
I remember where I was in a debate one day

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:57.440
in Drepung Monastery.

00:08:57.440 --> 00:09:01.740
And I heard this word BTAGS
PA MTHA' BZUNG GI RIGS PA.

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:05.320
BTAGS PA MTHA' BZUNG GI RIGS
PA means theoretical argument.

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:06.260
Theoretical case.

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:10.350
In the theoretical case that
something had a self-nature,

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:13.917
it should have these two qualities. What?

00:09:13.917 --> 00:09:16.330
BCOS MIN, it shouldn't
be artificially created,

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:19.050
and it should be GZHAN LA LTOS PA MED PA

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:20.450
It should not

00:09:22.441 --> 00:09:24.700
rely on other conditions.

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:28.620
So can such a nature exist?

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:30.413
That's another debate. Got it?

00:09:30.413 --> 00:09:34.221
So in theory, we say in theory, right?

00:09:34.221 --> 00:09:36.120
In theory, this is what
a self-nature would be.

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:39.370
You know, in practices, is there
such a thing? We don't know.

00:09:40.333 --> 00:09:45.308
And Choney Lama also
expresses his opinion.

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:49.240
And this is a very
traditional ancient opinion

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:52.870
on what a self-nature would
look like if it existed,

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:54.310
and it should have three qualities.

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:55.730
Here we go.

00:09:55.730 --> 00:09:57.171
Number one.

00:09:58.682 --> 00:09:59.515
GNYUG MA'I NGO BO

00:09:59.515 --> 00:10:00.348
GNYUG MA'I NGO BO

00:10:01.437 --> 00:10:04.120
GNYUG MA is a very, very, rare,

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:09.120
important word that means
from the beginningless.

00:10:09.253 --> 00:10:10.650
[laughing]

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:12.002
GNYUG MA

00:10:12.002 --> 00:10:12.940
It sounds like SMYUG MA

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:16.016
meaning a "bamboo shoot", but it's not.

00:10:16.016 --> 00:10:18.700
GNYUG MA means primeval,

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:21.961
primordial, since forever.

00:10:21.961 --> 00:10:24.860
GNYUG MAGNYUG MA'I NGO BO

00:10:24.860 --> 00:10:29.030
If something is the nature of fire,

00:10:29.030 --> 00:10:32.830
it should have been in
fires since forever.

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:33.911
Okay?

00:10:33.911 --> 00:10:36.332
Meaning hot, heat.

00:10:36.332 --> 00:10:38.380
If something is...

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:43.380
If fire has a nature, then a
self-nature or an identity,

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:46.150
then it should have always
been in those things

00:10:46.150 --> 00:10:49.370
as long as fires ever were.

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:51.200
That's the first thing.

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:53.820
Fires should have been hot since forever.

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:55.753
Number two.

00:10:56.990 --> 00:11:01.680
No matter whether you're talking
about a fire 100 years ago,

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:03.930
or a fire 100 years from now,

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:08.263
or a fire in this room right
now, it should be invariable.

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:11.420
The identity should always be there.

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:14.510
Whether you're talking about
fire 100 years from now,

00:11:14.510 --> 00:11:15.840
or a fire a hundred years ago,

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:18.003
or a fire in this present instant,

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:21.883
that identity should always be there.

00:11:22.850 --> 00:11:24.480
Hot.

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:25.513
Number three.

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:31.300
It should not be dependent on other

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:35.190
sources for its identity.

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:37.790
And he gives an interesting example.

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:41.398
You don't have to put a
hot water bottle on a fire.

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:46.100
Me and Veronica, we have
this cool thing nowadays

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:47.430
that somebody gave a,

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:49.913
it's cherry pits?

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:53.043
In a bag?

00:11:54.340 --> 00:11:57.360
And it has lavender flowers in there,

00:11:57.360 --> 00:12:00.530
and you put it in the
microwave and you heat it up,

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:01.880
and then you lie down on it.

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:04.220
It's very pleasant when you go to bed.

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:07.529
It stays warm for like
half an hour or something,

00:12:07.529 --> 00:12:10.026
and then it slowly gets cooler,
and you fall asleep on it.

00:12:10.026 --> 00:12:12.601
It's very pleasant, so...

00:12:14.069 --> 00:12:17.180
That's kind of like a hot water bottle.

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:18.463
So he says,

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:24.208
if fire is hot from the inside

00:12:24.208 --> 00:12:26.768
and you don't have to warm up

00:12:26.768 --> 00:12:28.723
the fire with a hot water bottle.

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:34.520
It's a bunny with cherry pits
and lavender inside of it.

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:37.850
If you don't need a cherry
pit lavender bunny heat up

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:40.180
in the microwave to make you warm,

00:12:40.180 --> 00:12:44.319
you're probably warmed by nature.

00:12:44.319 --> 00:12:46.053
Got it?

00:12:46.053 --> 00:12:47.150
Those are the three requirements.

00:12:47.150 --> 00:12:50.150
Again, it's probably BTAGS
PA MTHA' BZUNG GI RIGS PA

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:54.203
Here's a woman touching a candle flame.

00:12:55.090 --> 00:12:57.650
And one thing you can say about the...

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:00.180
One thing you automatically think is

00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:02.600
I hope she didn't put her finger in it

00:13:02.600 --> 00:13:04.300
because it would burn her.

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:06.960
Its nature is to be hot.

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:08.723
All right, next verse.

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:18.730
This is some kind of other
ideas about identity.

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:24.863
You know, my main thing about
identity is those three ideas.

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:29.290
But let's talk about some other things.

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:31.790
Let's talk about some
other characteristics

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:34.822
of the concept of identity.

00:13:34.822 --> 00:13:36.196
,RANG BZHIN YOD PA MA YIN NA,

00:13:36.196 --> 00:13:38.810
,GZHAN GYI DNGOS PO GA LA YOD,

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:42.415
This is very complex.

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:47.620
If you think about it,
fire has two natures.

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:52.093
One is inherent and one is adventitious.

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:56.390
Its color, for example.

00:13:56.390 --> 00:14:00.523
Adventitious means it depends
on outside circumstances.

00:14:01.702 --> 00:14:04.240
So which chemical did you...

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:06.350
What chemicals are in the wood

00:14:06.350 --> 00:14:08.330
will make a different color of flame.

00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:10.150
But the heat is there.

00:14:10.150 --> 00:14:12.980
The heat is the identity of fire,

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:16.005
and the color is secondary.

00:14:16.005 --> 00:14:17.550
It's a secondary characteristic.

00:14:17.550 --> 00:14:19.870
The secondary characteristics of fire

00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:22.950
can be created by other forces.

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:26.810
The self-identity or fire
should come from the inside.

00:14:26.810 --> 00:14:31.810
So nobody made a fire hot,
but you can change the color

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:35.500
by sprinkling different chemicals in it.

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:38.260
And everything about the fire

00:14:38.260 --> 00:14:40.647
is contained in those two things.

00:14:40.647 --> 00:14:44.630
Either it's natural identity
or it's a characteristic,

00:14:44.630 --> 00:14:48.361
which is imparted by other
circumstances, like its color.

00:14:49.369 --> 00:14:50.535
,GZHAN GYI DNGOS PO GA LA YOD,

00:14:50.535 --> 00:14:52.906
And there's nothing else about a fire.

00:14:52.906 --> 00:14:54.488
,GZHAN GYI DNGOS PO'I RANG BZHIN NI,

00:14:54.488 --> 00:14:57.138
,GZHAN GYI DNGOS PO YIN ZHES BRJOD,

00:15:00.218 --> 00:15:03.830
What do you call a nature that
comes from somewhere else?

00:15:03.830 --> 00:15:05.960
When the other person thinks of a nature

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:09.810
from somewhere else, we would say

00:15:09.810 --> 00:15:13.370
you're talking about a
self-existent somewhere else.

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:14.970
- What do you mean?

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:18.070
- Does the color of the fire
depend on an outside source?

00:15:18.070 --> 00:15:18.903
- Yes.

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:21.810
But when you say that,

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:24.910
you think the chemicals made the color.

00:15:24.910 --> 00:15:25.743
Got it?

00:15:28.259 --> 00:15:32.630
- Is the color of the fire
part of it natural identity?

00:15:32.630 --> 00:15:35.700
- No, it can change
according to chemicals.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:39.130
If you put sprinkled chemicals
on a fire and it changes

00:15:39.130 --> 00:15:42.460
the color of the fire,
that's adventitious.

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:43.833
That's, you know, secondary.

00:15:43.833 --> 00:15:47.603
That's created by outside forces.

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:52.290
But when you hear me say that,

00:15:52.290 --> 00:15:56.480
you think it comes from the
chemicals and that's a problem.

00:15:56.480 --> 00:15:59.980
You're even messing up the secondary ones.

00:16:00.967 --> 00:16:02.660
Forget that the fire is
hot from its own side

00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:04.290
which it's not.

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:06.890
It's hot from your side.

00:16:06.890 --> 00:16:09.520
But forget that supposed identity.

00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:12.370
You even misunderstand
why it changes color.

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:14.887
You think it's the chemicals.

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:16.880
Got it?

00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:19.420
And there's nothing else
about the fire, by the way.

00:16:19.420 --> 00:16:20.403
That's all there is.

00:16:20.403 --> 00:16:22.905
There's what it is and there's
this stuff it could be.

00:16:23.949 --> 00:16:26.702
And you don't understand either one.

00:16:28.071 --> 00:16:30.620
,RANG BZHIN DANG NI GZHAN DNGOS DAG,

00:16:30.620 --> 00:16:32.810
,MA GTOGS DNGOS PO GA LA YOD,

00:16:32.810 --> 00:16:36.860
There's no other fire than the one

00:16:36.860 --> 00:16:41.660
which is its natural identity
combined with its other

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:44.060
characteristics that are
created by other forces.

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:46.450
There's no other fire than that.

00:16:46.450 --> 00:16:48.950
Once you've covered those
two, that's the whole fire.

00:16:48.950 --> 00:16:50.530
And you don't understand either one,

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:53.900
therefore you don't understand the fire.

00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:54.975
All right.

00:16:54.975 --> 00:16:57.341
,RANG BZHIN DANG NI GZHAN DNGOS DAG,

00:16:57.341 --> 00:16:59.240
,YOD NA DNGOS PO 'GRUB PAR 'GYUR,

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:00.413
Anyway.

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:03.550
And here's where he says, you know,

00:17:03.550 --> 00:17:05.830
you don't understand the RANG BZHIN

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:08.100
and you don't understand the GZHAN DNGOS.

00:17:08.100 --> 00:17:11.460
You don't understand the
basic nature of the fire,

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:14.536
its own self-nature,
and you don't understand

00:17:14.536 --> 00:17:17.390
why it's moving or why it has
different colors or stuff,

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:21.157
or why it's different
temperature. You don't understand.

00:17:22.044 --> 00:17:25.323
,YOD NA DNGOS PO 'GRUB PAR 'GYUR,

00:17:25.323 --> 00:17:29.698
If the identity of the fire
and the characteristics

00:17:29.698 --> 00:17:32.690
of the fire existed the
way you think they do,

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:35.268
it couldn't be a fire.

00:17:35.268 --> 00:17:37.130
,GAL TE DNGOS PO MA GRUB NA,

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:39.788
If there was no real fire,

00:17:39.788 --> 00:17:42.170
,DNGOS MED 'GRUB PAR MI 'GYUR RO,

00:17:42.170 --> 00:17:47.170
then you couldn't have
the concept of unreal.

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:53.580
If there's no real fire, then
it's difficult to define unreal.

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:58.800
If there's no real cream
on the table, there's no...

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:03.600
It's difficult for my teacher
to say that's fake cream.

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:05.480
The powder is fake cream.

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:09.420
If he's never seen the
real cream, he can't...

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:11.777
The real cream defines the fake cream,

00:18:11.777 --> 00:18:14.960
and the fake cream defines the real cream.

00:18:14.960 --> 00:18:19.430
He doesn't smile and say, ah, real cream

00:18:19.430 --> 00:18:22.400
if he never had the danger
of having fake cream.

00:18:23.305 --> 00:18:24.200
[laughing]

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:28.270
And it was always my
job to talk the waitress

00:18:28.270 --> 00:18:29.490
into giving him real cream.

00:18:29.490 --> 00:18:32.401
Oh my God, sometimes
that took half an hour.

00:18:35.357 --> 00:18:37.320
,DNGOS PO GZHAN DU GYUR PA NI,

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:39.820
When something changes
into something else,

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:41.300
we already talked about it.

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:44.903
When milk, for example,
transforms into yogurt,

00:18:45.956 --> 00:18:50.065
,DNGOS MED YIN PAR SKYE BO SMRA,

00:18:50.065 --> 00:18:51.840
SKYE BO SMRA means people say,

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:53.178
people in the world say.

00:18:53.178 --> 00:18:55.870
SKYE BO SMRA means
people in the world say.

00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:57.200
Then what did they say?

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:59.791
It's not what it used to be.

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:04.770
When milk changes into yogurt,

00:19:04.770 --> 00:19:07.630
how do people talk about the milk?

00:19:07.630 --> 00:19:10.363
They say, well, it's
not what it used to be.

00:19:10.363 --> 00:19:15.345
Now it's all hunky, and
before it was fluid.

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:26.763
And if you could say about
a thing that it used to be,

00:19:26.763 --> 00:19:29.236
then it doesn't have a nature.

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:33.460
That's not what it used to be.

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:36.160
It's not what it used to be means

00:19:36.160 --> 00:19:41.160
whatever changed wasn't
inherent, was not its identity.

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:45.023
The milk...

00:19:47.860 --> 00:19:50.243
When I look at the yogurt, I say the milk.

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:53.530
It's not milk anymore.

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:55.580
When you say it's not milk anymore,

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:58.380
you're saying something
about the identity of milk.

00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:00.970
You're saying that it can end.

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:03.500
You're saying that it
can drop its identity.

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:05.630
Then it's not inherent, is it?

00:20:05.630 --> 00:20:08.050
Then it must be coming
from somewhere else, right?

00:20:08.050 --> 00:20:10.290
Then it doesn't have an inherent identity.

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:12.910
All it has is these other
characteristics that are created

00:20:12.910 --> 00:20:16.440
by outside forces, such as
your your seeds in your mind.

00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:17.273
Got it?

00:20:18.930 --> 00:20:19.763
Okay.

00:20:20.720 --> 00:20:22.763
Then the picture of the real cream.

00:20:24.220 --> 00:20:26.022
I always see my teacher smiling

00:20:26.022 --> 00:20:28.605
when I look at the real cream.

00:20:30.209 --> 00:20:31.042
All right.

00:20:32.541 --> 00:20:34.158
Let's go to the next verse.

00:20:35.034 --> 00:20:37.050
,GANG DAG RANG BZHIN GZHAN DNGOS DANG,

00:20:37.050 --> 00:20:39.158
,DNGOS DANG DNGOS MED NYID LTA BA,

00:20:39.158 --> 00:20:40.982
,DE DAG SANGS RGYAS BSTAN PA LA,

00:20:40.982 --> 00:20:43.441
,DE NYID MTHONG BA MA YIN NO,

00:20:45.280 --> 00:20:47.561
This is this typical...

00:20:52.496 --> 00:20:54.077
GANG DAG RANG BZHIN GZHAN DNGOS

00:20:54.077 --> 00:20:57.412
Those are the two things:
RANG BZHIN and GZHAN DNGOS.

00:20:58.260 --> 00:21:02.051
RANG BZHIN means "its
identity", its natural identity.

00:21:02.051 --> 00:21:04.530
GZHAN DNGOS means its "additional

00:21:04.530 --> 00:21:08.927
characteristics" added on
by other circumstances.

00:21:08.927 --> 00:21:12.160
DANG, DNGOS DANG DNGOS MED NYID LTA BA,

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:15.793
Is it fake or is it real?

00:21:15.793 --> 00:21:19.720
Is it real cream or is it creamer?

00:21:20.930 --> 00:21:24.560
Is it something made from a
cow that tastes delicious,

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:29.483
or is it something created by powder?

00:21:29.483 --> 00:21:32.823
So he's making two sets
of distinctions here:

00:21:34.660 --> 00:21:39.660
its identity and its extra
characteristics that are variable;

00:21:39.773 --> 00:21:44.040
and then the real milk and the fake milk.

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:46.930
Two sets of differences, two differences.

00:21:46.930 --> 00:21:48.880
Two sets of differences.

00:21:48.880 --> 00:21:50.630
"When I described them to you,"

00:21:50.630 --> 00:21:52.546
Nagarjuna's talking to the other guy,

00:21:52.546 --> 00:21:55.957
"you still think they're
all self-existent."

00:21:55.957 --> 00:22:00.770
And when I say real or unreal,

00:22:00.770 --> 00:22:03.725
and by the way, I'll ask you a question.

00:22:05.860 --> 00:22:09.191
Is it true that real can only
be defined by the unreal?

00:22:12.920 --> 00:22:17.130
Is it true that identity,
natural identity can only be

00:22:17.130 --> 00:22:19.943
defined by characteristics
which come and go?

00:22:22.780 --> 00:22:25.730
Is it true that you have to see short

00:22:25.730 --> 00:22:29.833
to perceive tall, in Buddhism?

00:22:31.710 --> 00:22:34.750
Because there's a lot
of people will tell you,

00:22:34.750 --> 00:22:35.840
and I see this all the time,

00:22:35.840 --> 00:22:38.440
there's some Burmese school
or something in America.

00:22:39.330 --> 00:22:42.040
They're always talking about emptiness

00:22:42.040 --> 00:22:45.313
as meaning the result of comparison,

00:22:46.320 --> 00:22:48.650
that nothing is real by
itself because it has to be

00:22:48.650 --> 00:22:49.863
compared to something else.

00:22:49.863 --> 00:22:54.320
Is that emptiness? Is that
dependent origination?

00:22:54.320 --> 00:22:55.660
It's not.

00:22:55.660 --> 00:22:58.593
It has nothing to do with it.

00:22:58.593 --> 00:23:01.410
That whole explanation of
emptiness is ridiculous.

00:23:01.410 --> 00:23:03.030
Tall is not defined by short.

00:23:03.030 --> 00:23:06.230
Tall is defined by the
seeds for tall in your mind.

00:23:06.230 --> 00:23:07.390
That's all.

00:23:07.390 --> 00:23:09.760
You're going to have tall without short

00:23:09.760 --> 00:23:13.770
because you can have seeds for
tall in your mind without short.

00:23:13.770 --> 00:23:15.290
Tall doesn't depend on short.

00:23:15.290 --> 00:23:18.386
Tall depends on what you
did yesterday to somebody.

00:23:18.386 --> 00:23:19.427
[laughing]

00:23:20.328 --> 00:23:21.210
Got it?

00:23:21.210 --> 00:23:23.668
Things aren't what they are by comparison.

00:23:25.117 --> 00:23:27.980
Real is not defined by artificial.

00:23:27.980 --> 00:23:31.190
In Buddhism, in real Buddhism,

00:23:31.190 --> 00:23:36.050
an identity is not defined by temporary

00:23:36.050 --> 00:23:38.463
coming and going characteristics.

00:23:39.350 --> 00:23:43.440
Identity is defined by your seeds.

00:23:44.770 --> 00:23:45.821
All right.

00:23:45.821 --> 00:23:46.990
,DE DAG SANGS RGYAS BSTAN PA LA,

00:23:46.990 --> 00:23:51.990
If you think big is only big by comparison

00:23:52.720 --> 00:23:57.720
or identity is only identity
by comparison to adventitious

00:23:57.840 --> 00:24:00.710
or coming and going characteristics,

00:24:00.710 --> 00:24:03.527
people who say that -- DE DAG

00:24:03.527 --> 00:24:04.985
SANGS RGYAS BSTAN PA LA,

00:24:04.985 --> 00:24:08.250
,DE NYID MTHONG BA MA YIN

00:24:08.250 --> 00:24:11.632
They didn't MTHONG DE NYID -- tattva.

00:24:13.934 --> 00:24:16.180
tattva

00:24:16.180 --> 00:24:19.019
Yeah, they didn't see emptiness,

00:24:19.019 --> 00:24:21.375
DE BZHIN -- suchness.

00:24:21.375 --> 00:24:22.917
They didn't see... tattva means suchness,

00:24:22.917 --> 00:24:23.750
here.

00:24:25.021 --> 00:24:28.220
If you think things are only
what they are by comparison,

00:24:28.220 --> 00:24:31.260
in a way, then you're
thinking that identity

00:24:31.260 --> 00:24:34.320
comes from its own side
or identity comes from

00:24:34.320 --> 00:24:36.130
the side of comparison.

00:24:36.130 --> 00:24:41.130
And then you don't understand
the nature of things.

00:24:41.450 --> 00:24:43.520
It's a joke. Get it?

00:24:43.520 --> 00:24:46.987
You don't understand the nature,
the real nature of things.

00:24:46.987 --> 00:24:49.790
DE NYID -- the real nature of things.

00:24:49.790 --> 00:24:52.089
It's a joke.

00:24:52.089 --> 00:24:52.922
Okay?

00:24:54.030 --> 00:24:57.040
By the way, as taught in
the Buddha's teachings,

00:24:57.040 --> 00:24:59.520
SANGS RGYAS BSTAN PA LA in the third line,

00:24:59.520 --> 00:25:02.600
you don't understand
the Buddhist teachings.

00:25:02.600 --> 00:25:05.190
And I don't know.

00:25:05.190 --> 00:25:07.638
I got this picture for you guys.

00:25:10.830 --> 00:25:13.870
These are three guys with blindfolds on.

00:25:13.870 --> 00:25:16.250
And these are the guys who think...

00:25:16.250 --> 00:25:20.830
They have wrong ideas about
identity or self-existence,

00:25:20.830 --> 00:25:23.370
and they're kind of
wandering around in the dark.

00:25:23.370 --> 00:25:26.550
And I just wanted you to see this picture

00:25:26.550 --> 00:25:31.550
because I want you to
appreciate why does Nagarjuna

00:25:32.470 --> 00:25:36.550
keep saying, "They don't get
it, what the Buddha said."

00:25:36.550 --> 00:25:38.270
"They don't get it, what the Buddha said."

00:25:38.270 --> 00:25:40.120
Historically, why do you think

00:25:40.120 --> 00:25:43.465
he might be hung up on
this point, for $100?

00:25:43.465 --> 00:25:45.152
[woman speaking indistinctly]

00:25:45.152 --> 00:25:47.706
- Historically, historically.

00:25:53.250 --> 00:25:56.684
[woman speaking indistinctly]

00:25:56.684 --> 00:25:59.000
Why does he keep coming
back to this theme of

00:25:59.000 --> 00:26:01.525
"you don't get what the Buddha taught"?

00:26:01.525 --> 00:26:04.266
- [Ven.Jigme] Probably
because [indistinct].

00:26:05.870 --> 00:26:09.717
- Yeah, good. You got 50 bucks so far.

00:26:09.717 --> 00:26:14.026
Jigme said there was another
system that contradicted.

00:26:14.026 --> 00:26:15.330
- [Ven. Jigme] It was
popular [indistinct].

00:26:15.330 --> 00:26:17.935
- Was popular for how long, for $50?

00:26:17.935 --> 00:26:19.444
- [Jigme] 200 years.

00:26:19.444 --> 00:26:20.611
- 700 years.

00:26:20.611 --> 00:26:22.069
- [Ven. Jigme] Abhidharma.

00:26:22.069 --> 00:26:23.168
- Yeah, Abhidharma.

00:26:23.168 --> 00:26:26.526
For 700 years, people misunderstood.

00:26:27.590 --> 00:26:29.380
They quoted Buddha. They memorized Buddha.

00:26:29.380 --> 00:26:30.780
They could memorize.

00:26:30.780 --> 00:26:32.620
They could recite all those books.

00:26:32.620 --> 00:26:35.311
And according to Nick's
text, Professor Nick's text,

00:26:35.311 --> 00:26:37.477
Buddha kept, you know...

00:26:38.889 --> 00:26:43.803
the Abhidharma sutras, they
also describe emptiness.

00:26:43.803 --> 00:26:48.470
Nagarjuna proves in the 60
Verses that the original sutras

00:26:49.600 --> 00:26:53.090
that we call Hinayana also
talked about emptiness.

00:26:53.090 --> 00:26:54.670
He proves it.

00:26:54.670 --> 00:26:57.560
So imagine how frustrated is Nagarjuna.

00:26:57.560 --> 00:27:01.670
He's bucking 700 years
of misunderstanding.

00:27:01.670 --> 00:27:03.740
He's trying to stand up in front

00:27:03.740 --> 00:27:07.860
of a 700 year tidal wave by himself.

00:27:07.860 --> 00:27:12.343
"Hey guys, it's all wrong."
[imitates the wave crushing]

00:27:13.350 --> 00:27:15.520
So he has to keep going
back to the scriptures

00:27:15.520 --> 00:27:17.640
and saying, "You don't get it.

00:27:17.640 --> 00:27:19.560
"You guys just don't get it.

00:27:19.560 --> 00:27:20.690
That's not what he meant."

00:27:20.690 --> 00:27:22.320
Got it?

00:27:22.320 --> 00:27:27.244
Can't you hear 700 years of
frustration in his voice?

00:27:27.244 --> 00:27:28.077
All right.

00:27:28.077 --> 00:27:31.060
That's in the blind fold. It's
suppose to remind you again.

00:27:34.370 --> 00:27:38.090
Now we shift to a major,
major topic in Buddhism,

00:27:38.090 --> 00:27:40.020
extremely important.

00:27:40.020 --> 00:27:41.290
And I'm sorry it's halfway through

00:27:41.290 --> 00:27:43.153
the last class for today

00:27:43.153 --> 00:27:46.146
because everyone's tired, but here we go.

00:27:46.146 --> 00:27:48.179
,BCOM LDAN DNGOS DANG DNGOS MED PA,

00:27:48.179 --> 00:27:50.895
,MKHYEN PAS KA TA YA NA YI,

00:27:50.895 --> 00:27:52.820
,GDAM NGAG LAS NI YOD PA DANG,

00:27:52.820 --> 00:27:55.530
,MED PA GNYIS KA'ANG DGAG PA MDZAD,

00:27:55.530 --> 00:27:57.133
Very, very Nagarjuna.

00:27:58.170 --> 00:28:00.080
Very important.

00:28:00.080 --> 00:28:04.995
Very important for the two
husbands in the kitchen.

00:28:04.995 --> 00:28:09.590
BCOM 'DAS - Bhagavan - the Buddha said

00:28:09.590 --> 00:28:11.772
he understood MKHYEN PA.

00:28:11.772 --> 00:28:14.266
The Buddha understood
the difference between

00:28:14.266 --> 00:28:15.708
DNGOS and DNGOS MED.

00:28:15.708 --> 00:28:19.624
DNGOS and DNGOS MED here
means the real and the unreal.

00:28:21.751 --> 00:28:22.968
The Buddha understood the difference

00:28:22.968 --> 00:28:24.680
between real and unreal.

00:28:24.680 --> 00:28:26.850
The husband in the kitchen who is real,

00:28:26.850 --> 00:28:28.530
and the husband in the
kitchen who is unreal.

00:28:28.530 --> 00:28:30.380
He understood the difference.

00:28:30.380 --> 00:28:34.230
And in a book called "Personal
Advices to Katyayana",

00:28:34.230 --> 00:28:37.520
this is one of his favorite disciples.

00:28:37.520 --> 00:28:39.220
Katyayana.

00:28:39.220 --> 00:28:44.220
Katyayana is very important in the sutras

00:28:44.380 --> 00:28:47.100
about the Wheel of Life.

00:28:47.100 --> 00:28:50.780
He's there when they first
paint the Wheel of Life.

00:28:50.780 --> 00:28:54.010
Then he comes home and tells the story.

00:28:54.010 --> 00:28:58.070
So anyway, Buddha gave
private advices to Katyayana.

00:28:58.070 --> 00:29:00.727
I went looking for them.

00:29:00.727 --> 00:29:03.241
You find some, but they're not clear.

00:29:03.241 --> 00:29:05.516
LAS NI YOD PA DANG MED PA
GNYIS KA'ANG DGAG PA MDZAD

00:29:05.516 --> 00:29:07.747
The Buddha denied that things could exist,

00:29:07.747 --> 00:29:12.747
and the Buddha also denied
that things could not exist.

00:29:13.163 --> 00:29:15.590
The Buddha denied that things exist,

00:29:15.590 --> 00:29:18.610
and he denied that things can't exist.

00:29:18.610 --> 00:29:19.530
All right?

00:29:19.530 --> 00:29:22.000
And that's really a big Nagarjuna thing.

00:29:22.000 --> 00:29:23.760
Very, very important.

00:29:23.760 --> 00:29:27.710
It's very helpful in the
two husbands in the kitchen.

00:29:27.710 --> 00:29:32.710
For $100. Where's the
deny something exists

00:29:34.640 --> 00:29:38.010
and deny that something
doesn't exist, in the kitchen?

00:29:38.010 --> 00:29:40.456
You've got to get both to get the $100.

00:29:42.170 --> 00:29:44.090
What does exist in the kitchen

00:29:44.090 --> 00:29:46.307
and what doesn't exist in the kitchen?

00:29:48.735 --> 00:29:49.848
- [Ven.Jigme] The husband you created.

00:29:49.848 --> 00:29:51.703
- The husband you created exists.

00:29:51.703 --> 00:29:52.961
- [Ven.Jigme] And the
husband you didn't create...

00:29:52.961 --> 00:29:55.988
- Yeah, and the husband who's
not your fault, don't exist.

00:29:55.988 --> 00:29:59.440
To say that the one that
don't exist, does exist,

00:29:59.440 --> 00:30:02.330
is called the extreme of existing.

00:30:02.330 --> 00:30:06.683
And to say that the one who
does exist doesn't exist,

00:30:06.683 --> 00:30:09.050
it's called the extreme of non-existing.

00:30:09.050 --> 00:30:10.773
You went too far.

00:30:13.107 --> 00:30:15.900
If the husband in the
kitchen is not my fault,

00:30:15.900 --> 00:30:16.790
he don't exist.

00:30:16.790 --> 00:30:17.890
Sorry.

00:30:17.890 --> 00:30:20.420
If the husband in the
kitchen is not his fault,

00:30:20.420 --> 00:30:22.020
he don't exist at all.

00:30:23.345 --> 00:30:24.536
Got it?

00:30:26.041 --> 00:30:27.180
[woman speaking indistinctly]

00:30:27.180 --> 00:30:32.180
And because the husband in the
kitchen is my fault, he does exist.

00:30:32.780 --> 00:30:36.380
So the husband exists and
doesn't exist at the same time.

00:30:36.380 --> 00:30:38.673
To deny that he exists is a problem.

00:30:39.680 --> 00:30:43.543
To deny that the husband who
is your fault exists is wrong.

00:30:44.580 --> 00:30:46.280
And to deny that there's any husband

00:30:46.280 --> 00:30:48.313
in the kitchen at all is also wrong.

00:30:49.150 --> 00:30:50.510
Got it?

00:30:50.510 --> 00:30:51.550
Two extremes.

00:30:51.550 --> 00:30:53.230
We call it falling off a cliff.

00:30:53.230 --> 00:30:56.529
In fact, the picture here

00:30:56.529 --> 00:31:00.770
is of a bridge threading ...

00:31:00.770 --> 00:31:02.500
I was trying to find one in Arizona.

00:31:02.500 --> 00:31:03.363
I got lucky.

00:31:05.690 --> 00:31:07.760
This is called Middle Way.

00:31:07.760 --> 00:31:10.710
And you're trying to
thread your way through,

00:31:10.710 --> 00:31:12.820
doesn't exist and does exist.

00:31:12.820 --> 00:31:15.960
If you think the husband who's
not your fault does exist,

00:31:15.960 --> 00:31:18.200
you fell off one side.

00:31:18.200 --> 00:31:21.220
If you think there's no husband at all,

00:31:21.220 --> 00:31:23.700
then you fell off the other side.

00:31:23.700 --> 00:31:27.400
And here is the great
reference to that idea

00:31:27.400 --> 00:31:29.250
in all of Buddhist scripture.

00:31:29.250 --> 00:31:31.493
It's here.

00:31:31.493 --> 00:31:32.326
Yay.

00:31:33.810 --> 00:31:34.643
Okay.

00:31:34.643 --> 00:31:38.870
Which means a good place to
throw in a Sanskrit lesson.

00:31:38.870 --> 00:31:43.870
And I researched the
extreme of saying he exists,

00:31:46.410 --> 00:31:48.720
from his own side and the extreme

00:31:48.720 --> 00:31:51.553
of saying he doesn't exist at all.

00:31:52.763 --> 00:31:54.873
So those have special
technical terms in Buddhism,

00:31:55.850 --> 00:31:57.400
which is called YOD PA'I
MTHA' and MED PA'I MTHA'

00:31:57.400 --> 00:31:58.690
YOD  MTHA' and MED  MTHA'

00:31:58.690 --> 00:32:00.657
Say: YOD MTHA' [students repeat]

00:32:00.657 --> 00:32:01.490
MED MTHA' [students repeat]

00:32:01.490 --> 00:32:04.002
YOD MTHA' [students repeat]
MED MTHA'[students repeat]

00:32:04.002 --> 00:32:07.294
YOD PA'I MTHA' means the
extreme of saying he exists...

00:32:07.294 --> 00:32:09.552
[Students] from his side,

00:32:09.552 --> 00:32:11.694
from his side and not
because I yelled at my kids.

00:32:11.694 --> 00:32:12.920
That's called...

00:32:12.920 --> 00:32:15.120
By the way, I'm really thinking
the next book I write...

00:32:15.120 --> 00:32:17.990
I am going to write
the two husbands sutra.

00:32:18.950 --> 00:32:19.783
Okay.

00:32:19.783 --> 00:32:22.865
So bhūtah (bhutah), it's
called bhūtahkoṭi (bhutahkoti).

00:32:22.865 --> 00:32:24.462
Say 'bhutahkoti'

00:32:24.462 --> 00:32:28.130
bhutahkoti, bhutahkoti

00:32:28.130 --> 00:32:30.930
'bhutah' means he exists.

00:32:30.930 --> 00:32:34.265
'koti' means extreme or cliff.

00:32:34.265 --> 00:32:37.555
'koti' means cliff or extreme.

00:32:37.555 --> 00:32:41.970
'koti' also means 10 million,
but that's a different thing.

00:32:41.970 --> 00:32:43.170
Okay.

00:32:43.170 --> 00:32:47.273
So √bhū means to be, and it came from...

00:32:47.273 --> 00:32:49.440
in the Indo-European it's called √bheu,

00:32:49.440 --> 00:32:52.888
and we get the words be, build.

00:32:52.888 --> 00:32:55.750
Where is that Sanskrit lesson?

00:32:55.750 --> 00:32:57.620
Oh, I'm sorry. I must have left it out

00:32:57.620 --> 00:32:58.453
Oopsie.

00:32:59.700 --> 00:33:02.850
Be, build and physics
come from the root √bheu.

00:33:02.850 --> 00:33:03.683
Physics also.

00:33:03.683 --> 00:33:08.683
The PH in physics comes
from that root √bheu.

00:33:08.972 --> 00:33:10.700
'koti' I couldn't find much

00:33:10.700 --> 00:33:13.690
except cut, which means
the angle, sharp angle,

00:33:13.690 --> 00:33:16.068
something you fall off.

00:33:16.068 --> 00:33:21.068
And koṭika (kotika) is the
MU in the MU BZHI MU GSUM,

00:33:21.431 --> 00:33:22.789
for $30.

00:33:23.639 --> 00:33:26.042
MU BZHI MU GSUM?

00:33:26.042 --> 00:33:30.303
[woman speaking indistinctly]

00:33:30.303 --> 00:33:33.742
MU BZHI MU GSUM, MU BZHI MU GSUM?

00:33:33.742 --> 00:33:35.385
You know MU BZHI MU GSUM.

00:33:35.385 --> 00:33:36.910
[woman speaking indistinctly]

00:33:36.910 --> 00:33:41.060
- Yeah. What do you call? Permutations.

00:33:41.060 --> 00:33:42.510
Four permutations.

00:33:42.510 --> 00:33:44.400
So 20 bucks for that answer.

00:33:44.400 --> 00:33:47.200
It means four...

00:33:47.200 --> 00:33:50.740
It's like you're on a
table with four edges.

00:33:50.740 --> 00:33:52.889
Four possible combinations,

00:33:52.889 --> 00:33:55.050
Koti, that's called 'kotika'.

00:33:55.050 --> 00:33:56.210
All right, good.

00:33:56.210 --> 00:33:58.260
Then the opposite is?

00:33:58.260 --> 00:34:02.933
What's the opposite,
Christina, of bhutakoti?

00:34:02.933 --> 00:34:05.940
Abhūtakoṭi (abhutakoti), abhutakoti.

00:34:05.940 --> 00:34:08.100
Which means the extreme of thinking

00:34:08.100 --> 00:34:10.050
if he's not coming from his side,

00:34:10.050 --> 00:34:12.370
he doesn't exist in the kitchen.

00:34:12.370 --> 00:34:14.620
Which is also another extreme.

00:34:15.760 --> 00:34:18.440
Which of those two extremes is learned,

00:34:18.440 --> 00:34:22.273
and which of those two
extremes is inherent in people?

00:34:31.760 --> 00:34:35.160
The classical answer,
so you can chew on it,

00:34:35.160 --> 00:34:40.160
is that the extreme of saying
he doesn't exist at all

00:34:41.280 --> 00:34:44.880
comes from a bad explanation of emptiness.

00:34:44.880 --> 00:34:47.060
That is normally learned.

00:34:47.060 --> 00:34:48.920
If he's not what I thought he was,

00:34:48.920 --> 00:34:53.920
then he doesn't exist at all,
is most often said by people

00:34:54.120 --> 00:34:57.750
who didn't understand
what emptiness means.

00:34:57.750 --> 00:34:59.489
All right, here we go.

00:34:59.489 --> 00:35:01.072
Let's do some more.

00:35:05.459 --> 00:35:06.979
Next verse.

00:35:06.979 --> 00:35:09.312
,GAL TE RANG BZHIN GYIS YOD NA,

00:35:09.312 --> 00:35:11.891
,DE NI MED NYID MI 'GYUR RO,

00:35:11.891 --> 00:35:13.816
,RANG BZHIN GZHAN DU 'GYUR BA NI,

00:35:13.816 --> 00:35:15.332
,NAM YANG 'THAD PAR MI 'GYUR RO,

00:35:15.332 --> 00:35:16.860
This is two separate thoughts,

00:35:16.860 --> 00:35:21.075
and they are RANG LUGS,
they're our own system.

00:35:21.075 --> 00:35:23.220
GAL TE RANG BZHIN GYIS YOD NA

00:35:23.220 --> 00:35:26.630
If any entity existed to
some nature of its own,

00:35:26.630 --> 00:35:28.050
which means the kind of identity

00:35:28.050 --> 00:35:30.570
we've been talking about,

00:35:30.570 --> 00:35:34.983
then MED NYID MI 'GYUR RO
-- it could never change.

00:35:36.130 --> 00:35:37.385
Okay?

00:35:37.385 --> 00:35:39.750
If its identity was inherent,

00:35:39.750 --> 00:35:41.600
it could never change to something else,

00:35:41.600 --> 00:35:44.280
which means it could never stop,

00:35:44.280 --> 00:35:47.390
because that's also changing.

00:35:47.390 --> 00:35:51.750
So if things had an identity of their own,

00:35:51.750 --> 00:35:53.995
because the identity is permanent,

00:35:53.995 --> 00:35:56.830
the thing could never stop

00:35:56.830 --> 00:35:59.410
because it had a permanent identity.

00:35:59.410 --> 00:36:01.580
It's a very interesting idea.

00:36:01.580 --> 00:36:05.738
And he says it would be
like NAM MKHA' MI SGRIB PA

00:36:05.738 --> 00:36:06.956
- What's a SGRIB PA, Tim?

00:36:06.956 --> 00:36:09.564
Do you remember SGRIB PA?

00:36:09.564 --> 00:36:13.564
SGRIB PA, MA SGRIB

00:36:14.710 --> 00:36:17.840
To obscure, to cover.

00:36:18.930 --> 00:36:22.854
Then he says, Choney Lama says,

00:36:22.854 --> 00:36:24.440
NAM MKHA' MI SGRIB PA

00:36:24.440 --> 00:36:26.590
- What's that? What's NAM MKHA'?

00:36:26.590 --> 00:36:27.953
[woman speaking indistinctly]

00:36:27.953 --> 00:36:29.237
- No, not sky.

00:36:29.237 --> 00:36:30.970
- [Woman] Space.
- Empty space.

00:36:30.970 --> 00:36:32.040
You've got to say empty space.

00:36:32.040 --> 00:36:33.890
Four kinds of space.

00:36:33.890 --> 00:36:35.225
You've got to say empty space.

00:36:35.225 --> 00:36:36.830
Never changes.

00:36:36.830 --> 00:36:38.410
He says then everything...

00:36:38.410 --> 00:36:42.440
If things had identities,
then because the identities

00:36:42.440 --> 00:36:45.930
never change, those
things could never change,

00:36:45.930 --> 00:36:48.908
because if they changed, they
would lose their identity.

00:36:48.908 --> 00:36:52.470
And then that also means if
the identity lasts forever,

00:36:52.470 --> 00:36:54.200
the thing would have to last forever.

00:36:54.200 --> 00:36:56.870
And it would be like empty
space which lasts forever.

00:36:56.870 --> 00:36:59.180
Whether the Earth is in that space,

00:36:59.180 --> 00:37:01.680
whether the planet Earth is in that space,

00:37:01.680 --> 00:37:03.970
or whether you destroy the planet Earth,

00:37:03.970 --> 00:37:05.868
the space is always going to be there.

00:37:05.868 --> 00:37:09.980
MA SGRIB means it's open
and cannot be obstructed.

00:37:10.970 --> 00:37:14.397
It's not like a box. It's like the space.

00:37:14.397 --> 00:37:15.930
,RANG BZHIN GZHAN DU 'GYUR BA NI,

00:37:15.930 --> 00:37:18.371
,NAM YANG 'THAD PAR MI 'GYUR RO,

00:37:18.371 --> 00:37:22.770
So if the identity of
a thing never changed,

00:37:22.770 --> 00:37:25.780
the thing would last forever.

00:37:25.780 --> 00:37:28.100
If the identity of thing did change,

00:37:28.100 --> 00:37:31.090
then that's not much
of an identity, is it?

00:37:31.090 --> 00:37:32.480
If fire could get cold,

00:37:32.480 --> 00:37:37.440
then what's the use of having an identity?

00:37:37.440 --> 00:37:38.773
Got it?

00:37:42.100 --> 00:37:43.320
Then the other guy comes.

00:37:43.320 --> 00:37:44.563
And oh my God.

00:37:45.520 --> 00:37:47.850
First he puts us, and then
he puts the other guy,

00:37:47.850 --> 00:37:50.370
and he doesn't tell us he's switching.

00:37:50.370 --> 00:37:51.695
Okay, here we go.

00:37:51.695 --> 00:37:53.711
,RANG BZHIN YOD PA MA YIN NA,

00:37:53.711 --> 00:37:56.670
,GZHAN DU 'GYUR PA GANG GI YIN,

00:37:58.490 --> 00:38:03.120
If the milk's nature could never change,

00:38:03.120 --> 00:38:06.362
then where did the yogurt come from?

00:38:09.130 --> 00:38:12.763
If the milk's nature could never change,

00:38:14.600 --> 00:38:18.507
then who turned into milk?

00:38:18.507 --> 00:38:20.520
Who turned into yogurt? Sorry.

00:38:20.520 --> 00:38:22.713
If the milk's nature could never change,

00:38:23.770 --> 00:38:26.103
then who turned into yogurt?

00:38:27.380 --> 00:38:30.643
And then we say,

00:38:33.473 --> 00:38:38.037
if the milk could have a
nature, then what changes?

00:38:40.350 --> 00:38:41.183
Okay?

00:38:41.183 --> 00:38:42.458
It's called RIGS PA MGO MTSHUNGS

00:38:42.458 --> 00:38:44.130
RIGS PA MGO MTSHUNGS
means parallel reasoning.

00:38:44.130 --> 00:38:45.540
I'll say it again.

00:38:45.540 --> 00:38:46.690
He says...

00:38:48.650 --> 00:38:50.380
Sorry, I've got to look at it.

00:38:50.380 --> 00:38:53.350
If things don't have
a nature of their own,

00:38:53.350 --> 00:38:58.070
then how can you say it
changed into something else?

00:38:58.070 --> 00:39:00.110
If milk doesn't have a nature,

00:39:00.110 --> 00:39:03.228
how can you say the
milk turned into yogurt?

00:39:05.430 --> 00:39:08.140
If the milk doesn't
have a certain identity,

00:39:08.140 --> 00:39:11.603
how can you say it
changed to something else?

00:39:13.820 --> 00:39:16.560
If you don't have a driver's
license to start with,

00:39:16.560 --> 00:39:19.660
how can you say you got
a fake driver's license?

00:39:20.610 --> 00:39:23.740
How's that? [laughing]

00:39:23.740 --> 00:39:25.050
That's the other guy.

00:39:25.050 --> 00:39:27.430
And then we say, "No, you don't get it.

00:39:27.430 --> 00:39:31.003
If it does have an identity,
then it couldn't change."

00:39:32.370 --> 00:39:33.740
Don't tell me it couldn't change

00:39:33.740 --> 00:39:36.930
if it didn't have an identity,
which is his argument.

00:39:36.930 --> 00:39:38.830
If it's not something, how can it change?

00:39:38.830 --> 00:39:40.840
And we say, "No, you don't get it.

00:39:40.840 --> 00:39:42.740
If it is something, how can it change?"

00:39:43.821 --> 00:39:44.810
[laughing]

00:39:44.810 --> 00:39:46.827
Got it? Cute?

00:39:47.970 --> 00:39:48.803
Confusing.

00:39:48.803 --> 00:39:52.731
Halfway through the second
half, we switched to us.

00:39:54.048 --> 00:39:55.548
Thanks, Nagarjuna.

00:39:56.490 --> 00:39:57.323
All right.

00:39:57.323 --> 00:40:01.340
And I don't know.

00:40:01.340 --> 00:40:03.853
I forget why I put a sculptor here.

00:40:08.010 --> 00:40:09.187
Yeah.

00:40:09.187 --> 00:40:11.010
I mean, the idea is could you change

00:40:11.010 --> 00:40:15.532
something which was unchangeable,
or something like that?

00:40:15.532 --> 00:40:17.750
All right, here we go.

00:40:17.750 --> 00:40:20.017
Don't worry, we're getting there.

00:40:21.720 --> 00:40:24.690
The next verse is even more
famous than the last ones

00:40:24.690 --> 00:40:26.380
I told you were famous.

00:40:26.380 --> 00:40:28.593
This is the super famous verse.

00:40:29.551 --> 00:40:30.815
,YOD CES BYA BA RTAG PAR 'DZIN,

00:40:30.815 --> 00:40:33.489
Say YOD CES BYA BA [students repeat]

00:40:33.489 --> 00:40:35.347
RTAG PAR 'DZIN [students repeat]

00:40:35.347 --> 00:40:37.097
MED CES BYA BA [students repeat]

00:40:37.097 --> 00:40:38.991
CHAD PAR LTA [students repeat]

00:40:38.991 --> 00:40:40.499
DE PHYIR [students repeat]

00:40:40.499 --> 00:40:43.499
YOD DANG MED PA LA [students repeat]

00:40:43.499 --> 00:40:45.791
MKHAS PAS GNAS PAR [students Repeat]

00:40:45.791 --> 00:40:47.482
MI BYA'O [students repeat]

00:40:47.482 --> 00:40:51.000
If you think things exist,
you're falling into the extreme

00:40:51.000 --> 00:40:54.330
of thinking that things can never change.

00:40:54.330 --> 00:40:56.530
If you think that things don't exist,

00:40:56.530 --> 00:40:59.973
you're falling into the extreme
that things never started.

00:41:00.870 --> 00:41:05.870
Therefore, those of you who are masters

00:41:06.680 --> 00:41:09.170
should stay in the middle.

00:41:09.170 --> 00:41:11.740
And there's Middle Way.

00:41:11.740 --> 00:41:14.415
What's the nickname of Wisdom?

00:41:16.510 --> 00:41:18.861
Yeah, Middle Way.

00:41:18.861 --> 00:41:20.540
Madhyamika.

00:41:20.540 --> 00:41:24.100
That's the nickname of prajna.

00:41:24.100 --> 00:41:27.825
Where do you see that
nickname used? For $100.

00:41:29.164 --> 00:41:32.997
- [Christina] In the title
of Choney Lama's [indistinct]

00:41:35.050 --> 00:41:36.828
- You're close.

00:41:36.828 --> 00:41:37.900
- [Tim] Entering the Middle Way.

00:41:37.900 --> 00:41:40.832
- Yeah. $100 for Tim.

00:41:40.832 --> 00:41:43.120
$100 for Tim.

00:41:43.120 --> 00:41:43.953
Yeah.

00:41:45.240 --> 00:41:48.930
Chandrakirti did not call
his book Entering Wisdom.

00:41:48.930 --> 00:41:51.200
He called it Entering the Middle Way.

00:41:51.200 --> 00:41:55.850
But that middle way is
called Madhyamika Shastra,

00:41:55.850 --> 00:41:58.180
the commentary on the Middle Way.

00:41:58.180 --> 00:41:59.013
All right.

00:41:59.013 --> 00:42:00.310
So here it is.

00:42:00.310 --> 00:42:05.310
If you think things exist,
then they could never change.

00:42:05.750 --> 00:42:09.413
If you think things don't
exist, then you're a nihilist.

00:42:10.800 --> 00:42:11.633
Okay.

00:42:11.633 --> 00:42:16.625
Therefore, real wise men and women should

00:42:17.602 --> 00:42:20.070
stay somewhere between those two.

00:42:20.070 --> 00:42:22.790
You should stay between those two.

00:42:22.790 --> 00:42:25.541
What's that mean in the kitchen for $300?

00:42:26.600 --> 00:42:27.780
- [Pau] To understand that...

00:42:27.780 --> 00:42:28.810
- Go slow, go slow.

00:42:28.810 --> 00:42:30.311
This is a lot of money.

00:42:30.311 --> 00:42:32.110
[everybody laughing]

00:42:32.110 --> 00:42:33.880
Where's the Middle Way in the kitchen?

00:42:33.880 --> 00:42:38.880
- [Pau] When you understand that
if the husband is yelling at you,

00:42:39.263 --> 00:42:44.254
it's because you yelled
at their kids last week.

00:42:45.169 --> 00:42:46.252
- Good.

00:42:47.457 --> 00:42:50.307
And therefore, that's exists.

00:42:50.307 --> 00:42:52.312
What doesn't exist in the kitchen?

00:42:52.312 --> 00:42:56.253
- [Pau] The husband that
"because I didn't do anything."

00:42:56.253 --> 00:42:59.222
- That "I didn't do anything
husband" doesn't exist, yeah.

00:42:59.222 --> 00:43:01.230
So stay between those two places.

00:43:01.230 --> 00:43:02.607
Got it?

00:43:02.607 --> 00:43:05.178
$300.

00:43:05.178 --> 00:43:07.180
[mouth blowing]

00:43:07.180 --> 00:43:09.499
She's taking you out to dinner Pachi.

00:43:09.499 --> 00:43:10.514
Okay.

00:43:10.514 --> 00:43:12.516
[man speaking indistinctly]

00:43:12.516 --> 00:43:14.300
Okay, good.

00:43:14.300 --> 00:43:15.849
,GANG ZHIG RANG BZHIN GYIS YOD PA,

00:43:15.849 --> 00:43:17.815
,DE NI MED PA MIN PAS RTAG,

00:43:17.815 --> 00:43:20.389
,SNGON BYUNG DA LTAR MED CES PA,

00:43:20.389 --> 00:43:22.897
,DES NA CHAD PAR THAL BAR 'GYUR.

00:43:22.897 --> 00:43:23.730
Okay.

00:43:23.730 --> 00:43:24.840
And he expands on the meaning

00:43:24.840 --> 00:43:29.570
of unchanging and never starting.

00:43:29.570 --> 00:43:33.710
By the way, these two extremes,

00:43:33.710 --> 00:43:38.710
unchanging and discontinuing,
these two extremes

00:43:39.080 --> 00:43:42.610
are described as the
result of certain opinions.

00:43:42.610 --> 00:43:45.560
They're always described as
the result of certain opinions.

00:43:46.440 --> 00:43:51.405
If the husband was
coming from his own side,

00:43:52.930 --> 00:43:56.286
he could never change -- RTAG PA.

00:43:56.286 --> 00:43:59.579
And what's the other one?

00:43:59.579 --> 00:44:01.380
CHAD PA

00:44:01.380 --> 00:44:04.710
If he, I guess if he is coming,

00:44:04.710 --> 00:44:09.510
Oh, if he's not coming from
his own side, he can't exist.

00:44:09.510 --> 00:44:11.763
Then he'd just stop.

00:44:13.248 --> 00:44:14.807
Got it?

00:44:15.730 --> 00:44:16.563
All right.

00:44:16.563 --> 00:44:20.573
And I have a special
picture I made for you guys.

00:44:21.410 --> 00:44:26.165
The Middle Way to the two husbands.

00:44:29.136 --> 00:44:29.969
Okay?

00:44:30.885 --> 00:44:34.350
So if you think he's
just from his own side,

00:44:34.350 --> 00:44:37.228
you fell off the right side of the bridge.

00:44:37.228 --> 00:44:39.470
If you think, if he doesn't
come from his own side,

00:44:39.470 --> 00:44:42.790
he can't exist, you fell off
the left side of the bridge.

00:44:42.790 --> 00:44:45.210
And if you stay in the middle way,

00:44:45.210 --> 00:44:47.508
you have this happy relationship.

00:44:48.561 --> 00:44:49.417
Yay!

00:44:52.650 --> 00:44:54.010
Oh, I'm so sorry.

00:44:54.010 --> 00:44:57.491
That's the last picture in the class.

00:44:57.491 --> 00:44:59.520
So let's summarize.

00:44:59.520 --> 00:45:01.690
What was the name of this chapter?

00:45:01.690 --> 00:45:04.330
We were discussing identity.

00:45:04.330 --> 00:45:08.690
Could a thing, could something
have an identity of its own?

00:45:08.690 --> 00:45:13.690
And we decided it could not
have an identity of its own

00:45:14.250 --> 00:45:18.370
because even those
characteristics of things

00:45:18.370 --> 00:45:21.890
like the heat of fire, that
seemed to be in the fire,

00:45:21.890 --> 00:45:24.010
are coming from us.

00:45:24.010 --> 00:45:25.460
That's the bottom line.

00:45:25.460 --> 00:45:28.560
So there is no natural
identity to anything.

00:45:29.670 --> 00:45:30.503
Okay.

00:45:30.503 --> 00:45:33.867
Oh, what's that mean about
Medicine Buddha mantras?

00:45:35.173 --> 00:45:36.300
[woman speaking indistinctly]

00:45:36.300 --> 00:45:38.658
Yeah, suppose you had a bad motivation and

00:45:38.658 --> 00:45:41.000
you did a Medicine Buddha Mantra?

00:45:41.000 --> 00:45:42.150
What would happen then?

00:45:42.150 --> 00:45:43.663
That's a sign of the,

00:45:44.700 --> 00:45:47.470
of the identity of the mantra.

00:45:47.470 --> 00:45:50.803
Does it have an identity
of being beneficial?

00:45:51.760 --> 00:45:52.969
No.

00:45:52.969 --> 00:45:56.350
If you say those mantras
with a competitive attitude,

00:45:56.350 --> 00:45:58.270
then they could hurt somebody, right?

00:45:58.270 --> 00:45:59.103
Cool?

00:45:59.103 --> 00:46:01.450
That's the emptiness of the mantras.

00:46:01.450 --> 00:46:04.243
They don't have an identity of their own.

00:46:05.680 --> 00:46:06.513
Cool.

00:46:06.513 --> 00:46:08.738
See you next time. Yay!

